1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,953
In this lesson, we'll define parabolas
geometrically, using a focus and a

2
00:00:04,953 --> 00:00:05,632
directrix.

3
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:12,061
A parabola is every point that is the same
distance from a fixed point, the focus,

4
00:00:12,061 --> 00:00:14,127
and a fixed line, the directrix.

5
00:00:14,577 --> 00:00:16,603
The vertex sits halfway between them.

6
00:00:17,733 --> 00:00:23,728
With vertex at the origin opening up, the
equation is x squared equals four p y.

7
00:00:24,178 --> 00:00:30,489
p is the distance from the vertex to the
focus. Opening sideways, it's y squared

8
00:00:30,489 --> 00:00:31,751
equals four p x.

9
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:38,041
For x squared equals twelve y, four p
equals twelve, so p equals three.

10
00:00:38,491 --> 00:00:43,505
The focus is zero, three and the directrix
is y equals negative three.

11
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:50,579
A parabola has vertex two, negative one
and focus two, one. Then p equals two,

12
00:00:50,579 --> 00:00:51,417
opening up.

13
00:00:51,867 --> 00:00:56,689
The equation is x minus two squared equals
eight times y plus one.

14
00:00:57,833 --> 00:01:03,183
Every ray coming in parallel to the axis
reflects off the parabola straight through

15
00:01:03,183 --> 00:01:03,828
the focus.

16
00:01:04,278 --> 00:01:08,161
That's why satellite dishes and car
headlights are parabolic.

17
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:13,737
Your turn. Find the focus of y squared
equals negative eight x.

18
00:01:14,187 --> 00:01:15,723
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:16,173 --> 00:01:22,128
Four p equals negative eight, so p is
negative two. The focus is negative two,

20
00:01:22,128 --> 00:01:22,509
zero.

21
00:01:23,633 --> 00:01:27,025
In this lesson, we'll study ellipses, the
stretched circles.

22
00:01:28,166 --> 00:01:33,478
An ellipse is every point whose distances
to two foci add up to the same total.

23
00:01:33,928 --> 00:01:37,512
Tie a string to two pins and trace around
them with a pencil.

24
00:01:37,633 --> 00:01:44,470
Centered at the origin, the equation is x
squared over a squared plus y squared over

25
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:45,929
b squared equals one.

26
00:01:46,379 --> 00:01:49,920
a is half the long axis and b is half the
short axis.

27
00:01:51,066 --> 00:01:56,677
The foci are c units from the center,
where c squared equals a squared minus b

28
00:01:56,677 --> 00:01:57,253
squared.

29
00:01:57,703 --> 00:02:03,785
For x squared over twenty five plus y
squared over nine equals one, c squared is

30
00:02:03,785 --> 00:02:07,815
sixteen, so the foci are at plus or minus
four, zero.

31
00:02:08,933 --> 00:02:14,743
Complete the square to find the center.
Four x squared plus y squared minus

32
00:02:14,743 --> 00:02:18,384
sixteen x plus two y plus thirteen equals
zero.

33
00:02:18,834 --> 00:02:25,230
It becomes x minus two squared over one
plus y plus one squared over four equals

34
00:02:25,230 --> 00:02:29,308
one: center two, negative one, vertical
major axis.

35
00:02:30,433 --> 00:02:34,956
Eccentricity e equals c over a measures
how stretched the ellipse is.

36
00:02:35,406 --> 00:02:41,400
Near zero, it's almost a circle. Earth's
orbit has e about point zero one seven.

37
00:02:42,533 --> 00:02:48,401
Your turn. Find the vertices of x squared
over sixteen plus y squared over thirty

38
00:02:48,401 --> 00:02:49,488
six equals one.

39
00:02:49,938 --> 00:02:51,474
Pause the video and try it.

40
00:02:51,924 --> 00:02:57,790
The bigger denominator is under y, so the
vertices are zero, plus or minus six.

41
00:02:58,933 --> 00:03:03,264
In this lesson, we'll study hyperbolas,
the conics with two branches.

42
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:10,074
A hyperbola is every point whose distances
to two foci differ by the same amount.

43
00:03:10,524 --> 00:03:14,044
It has two separate branches, opening away
from each other.

44
00:03:15,166 --> 00:03:20,870
Centered at the origin and opening left
and right, the equation is x squared over

45
00:03:20,870 --> 00:03:24,532
a squared minus y squared over b squared
equals one.

46
00:03:24,982 --> 00:03:27,840
The vertices are at plus or minus a, zero.

47
00:03:28,966 --> 00:03:33,553
The asymptotes are y equals plus or minus
b over a times x.

48
00:03:34,003 --> 00:03:38,974
Draw a box with sides two a and two b; the
diagonals are the asymptotes.

49
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:43,897
For hyperbolas, c squared equals a squared
plus b squared.

50
00:03:44,347 --> 00:03:50,976
For x squared over nine minus y squared
over sixteen equals one, c is five, so the

51
00:03:50,976 --> 00:03:57,443
foci are at plus or minus five, zero.
Asymptotes are y equals plus or minus four

52
00:03:57,443 --> 00:03:58,171
thirds x.

53
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:03,289
If the y term comes first, the hyperbola
opens up and down.

54
00:04:03,739 --> 00:04:10,529
y squared over four minus x squared equals
one has vertices zero, plus or minus two

55
00:04:10,529 --> 00:04:14,128
and asymptotes y equals plus or minus two
x.

56
00:04:15,266 --> 00:04:21,535
Your turn. Find the foci of x squared over
sixteen minus y squared over nine equals

57
00:04:21,535 --> 00:04:21,837
one.

58
00:04:22,287 --> 00:04:23,823
Pause the video and try it.

59
00:04:24,273 --> 00:04:29,244
c squared is twenty five, so the foci are
at plus or minus five, zero.

60
00:04:30,366 --> 00:04:35,123
In this lesson, we'll identify a conic
just by looking at its equation.

61
00:04:36,266 --> 00:04:42,870
Every conic can be written A x squared
plus C y squared plus D x plus E y plus F

62
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:43,861
equals zero.

63
00:04:44,311 --> 00:04:48,748
The coefficients A and C, on the squared
terms, tell you which one it is.

64
00:04:49,866 --> 00:04:51,679
If A equals C, it's a circle.

65
00:04:52,129 --> 00:04:57,932
x squared plus y squared minus six x plus
four y equals three is a circle.

66
00:04:57,932 --> 00:05:03,500
Completing the square gives center three,
negative two and radius four.

67
00:05:04,633 --> 00:05:07,705
If only one variable is squared, it's a
parabola.

68
00:05:08,155 --> 00:05:14,363
y squared minus four x plus two y equals
seven is a parabola that opens sideways.

69
00:05:15,499 --> 00:05:21,074
If A and C have the same sign but differ,
it's an ellipse. Opposite signs give a

70
00:05:21,074 --> 00:05:21,771
hyperbola.

71
00:05:22,221 --> 00:05:28,576
Four x squared plus nine y squared equals
thirty six is an ellipse. Four x squared

72
00:05:28,576 --> 00:05:32,760
minus nine y squared equals thirty six is
a hyperbola.

73
00:05:33,899 --> 00:05:38,379
Try these. Two x squared plus two y
squared equals eight: a circle.

74
00:05:38,829 --> 00:05:45,493
x squared minus y squared plus four y
equals zero: a hyperbola. Three y squared

75
00:05:45,493 --> 00:05:48,024
plus x equals six: a parabola.

76
00:05:49,166 --> 00:05:55,118
Your turn. Identify five x squared plus y
squared minus ten x equals zero.

77
00:05:55,568 --> 00:05:57,104
Pause the video and try it.

78
00:05:57,554 --> 00:06:01,074
Both squared, same sign, different
coefficients: an ellipse.

